WEBVTT

00:03.080 --> 00:07.000
Let me ask you a question
that will hopefully make it up to you.

00:07.790 --> 00:10.790
Do you want to go somewhere even scarier?

00:11.830 --> 00:15.960
Hold up, Yayoi-chan! Castle H
was dangerous enough, and you wanna-

00:15.960 --> 00:16.670
Cause we can.

00:18.210 --> 00:22.830
The sealed-off haunt that's known for sightings
of a woman in a kimono.

00:23.540 --> 00:26.080
O City in Tokyo, the Old F Tunnel.

00:26.080 --> 00:28.330
<b>O City: Old F Tunnel</b>

00:26.080 --> 00:28.330
<b>Danger: S</b>

00:27.040 --> 00:31.040
Not another Rank S...

02:02.960 --> 02:04.500
So, with that out of the way...

02:06.920 --> 02:09.540
Know a good place to hide this?

02:09.540 --> 02:10.540
Huh?!

02:10.670 --> 02:13.380
Wait, you brought it back with you?!

02:13.380 --> 02:14.040
Yep.

02:14.040 --> 02:16.540
I-is that a real mummified arm?

02:17.000 --> 02:20.790
Hold on. Doesn't this count as mutilating a corpse?

02:20.790 --> 02:24.170
Y-yeah, we definitely don't want
to have it here at the house...

02:24.500 --> 02:26.040
Then Keitaro can put it in his room.

02:26.290 --> 02:29.330
So I can get arrested?!
I don't want it there in the first place!

02:29.920 --> 02:33.790
Why don't we find someplace to hide it
while we're out and about on our trip?

02:33.790 --> 02:35.170
Yeah, good idea!

02:35.170 --> 02:37.880
Did you have to pick the most normal option?

02:38.460 --> 02:39.920
I'll go get ready, then.

02:40.580 --> 02:42.330
T-take your time.

02:43.790 --> 02:44.630
So...

02:45.580 --> 02:48.130
Were you scared at that castle?

02:48.880 --> 02:50.380
Well, yeah.

02:50.380 --> 02:51.080
Uh-huh.

02:51.080 --> 02:53.330
Like, I'm ready to call this whole thing off.

02:54.130 --> 02:59.080
But of course we're gonna hit up a place
that's just as bad. I don't even wanna think about it.

02:59.080 --> 03:01.920
Aww, you had a pretty rough night, huh?

03:02.540 --> 03:03.460
But...

03:04.170 --> 03:06.130
...you must've loved it.

03:07.380 --> 03:09.250
Wh-what?

03:11.040 --> 03:13.750
Kei-kun, last time you had
a dangerous brush with the supernatural,

03:13.750 --> 03:16.250
you wanted to get away from it, right?

03:16.790 --> 03:17.710
Now, though...

03:18.420 --> 03:21.380
...you're choosing to involve yourself even further.

03:23.290 --> 03:27.750
I don't think you're doing that just to protect anyone.

03:28.580 --> 03:29.960
I think you're entranced by it.

03:31.670 --> 03:32.960
You must have felt it.

03:33.250 --> 03:36.170
That anticipation as you wait for something
mysterious to happen...

03:36.630 --> 03:40.920
The frantic rhythm of your pounding heart,
racing as fast as when you fall in love...

03:41.960 --> 03:47.040
The wave of pleasurable relief that crashes over you
when the danger has finally passed...

03:49.380 --> 03:52.290
You must have noticed how good it feels by now.

03:59.290 --> 04:02.380
Don't be scared. You don't need to be afraid.

04:03.250 --> 04:06.420
You're doing this to break our curse.

04:07.670 --> 04:09.920
So don't deny this part of yourself.

04:10.880 --> 04:12.500
Accept it for who you are.

04:14.080 --> 04:15.290
When she said...

04:15.920 --> 04:18.420
You love to feel fear.

04:18.830 --> 04:22.830
I quickly brushed off those words.

04:23.210 --> 04:24.750
But now...

04:25.500 --> 04:29.580
I'll be right here by your side to help you, Kei-kun.

04:31.540 --> 04:34.040
With her words and her fingers holding me in their grip,

04:34.580 --> 04:37.630
I can't find the will to deny them.

04:46.420 --> 04:49.130
That arm of ours really is long gone. Darn.

04:49.670 --> 04:52.210
So is the spirit that was bound here.

04:52.710 --> 04:56.630
They have been separated.

04:57.040 --> 05:00.130
Yes, because it certainly still exists.

05:00.540 --> 05:02.460
Goodness, gracious...

05:03.170 --> 05:05.500
You only had one job, Granny.

05:07.580 --> 05:12.790
I even got you a costume from the appropriate
historical era so you could keep watch.

05:13.170 --> 05:16.960
I expected a wandering ghost to do better.
Are you really that useless?

05:17.960 --> 05:19.670
Are you going to apologize?

05:23.170 --> 05:25.580
I'm afraid I can't hear you!

05:25.000 --> 05:25.630
<b>KANNON SHINKYO</b>

05:31.920 --> 05:35.500
Really? You shouldn't have forced it to pass on.

05:35.920 --> 05:38.920
We could have learned more from it.

05:40.290 --> 05:41.920
Forgive me, I couldn't help myself.

05:42.750 --> 05:45.540
I despise those who won't listen.

05:46.250 --> 05:48.170
That's the terrible thing about being a priest.

05:50.170 --> 05:52.000
No, you're just terrible.

05:52.460 --> 05:55.250
We must find it, no matter what.

05:56.250 --> 06:02.380
That relic is crucial to accomplishing our mission.

06:03.080 --> 06:05.380
I'll take care of it, then.

06:05.880 --> 06:09.130
I'll reach out to the national network of crooked clergy.

06:09.830 --> 06:16.790
Hurry, then. We must assemble its power-infused body
and bring forth its spirit.

06:17.080 --> 06:18.830
No need to hurry.

06:19.250 --> 06:22.080
Besides, it's still has more growing to do.

06:22.540 --> 06:27.080
Speaking of, I wonder what it's up to right now...

06:27.830 --> 06:30.630
Our all-powerful spirit...

06:35.500 --> 06:37.710
...the Seed of the Moonless Dawn.

06:51.540 --> 06:53.920
HURRY AND KILL IT!

06:55.630 --> 06:57.040
Kill it!

06:57.130 --> 07:00.670
KILL IT, KILL IT, KILL IT! KILL IT, KILL IT, KILL IT!

07:05.960 --> 07:07.670
It's just a baby.

07:08.210 --> 07:12.880
THAT MAKES IT EASIER TO STRANGLE!

07:12.880 --> 07:15.170
KILL IT!

07:31.130 --> 07:39.880
Two powerful spirits: The Seed of the Moonless Dawn,
AKA the "Spectre of Death," and Kishimojin.

07:40.630 --> 07:45.880
For reasons yet unknown,
a clash between them was narrowly avoided.

07:46.830 --> 07:48.000
However...

07:51.000 --> 07:54.080
...It acknowledged its powerful presence.

07:54.670 --> 07:56.380
And in the near future,

07:57.290 --> 08:01.040
they would come to meet once again.

08:13.000 --> 08:14.750
Yayoi-chan, you ready?

08:14.750 --> 08:17.330
Yeah. You look geared up.

08:18.500 --> 08:22.380
I got myself a special uniform
for taking on spooky haunts!

08:22.380 --> 08:23.540
I'm gonna be sick...

08:23.710 --> 08:28.670
I can't believe we're going to an S-Rank haunt,
the Old F Tunnel!

08:28.670 --> 08:30.130
I've never been this excited!

08:30.130 --> 08:30.580
Same.

08:30.580 --> 08:33.420
Okay, it's spooky adventure time!

08:33.420 --> 08:34.710
Let's ghooo...

08:34.710 --> 08:35.790
...ooost!

08:35.790 --> 08:37.670
I haven't heard that in ages!

08:40.040 --> 08:41.210
Setting up GPS.

08:43.040 --> 08:44.380
Wait, I know that doll!

08:44.790 --> 08:47.250
I thought I dropped that and left it behind...

08:47.250 --> 08:47.960
You did.

08:48.380 --> 08:50.540
You need to go back and pick it up next time.

08:50.630 --> 08:51.920
S-sorry...

08:52.670 --> 08:53.880
Or else, someone could die.

08:54.250 --> 08:56.170
I-I'll be more careful!

08:56.710 --> 08:58.080
Speaking of, Eiko.

08:59.210 --> 09:02.920
I want to stop somewhere before we head to the tunnel.

09:02.920 --> 09:05.330
Okay, but why?

09:05.750 --> 09:08.540
I wanna pick up another Graduate.

09:08.750 --> 09:12.380
Wait, what? Is the one we have not enough?

09:12.750 --> 09:17.710
It exhausted a lot of power yesterday, 
plus we'll want backup in case it goes rogue again.

09:18.460 --> 09:26.040
I picked the Old F Tunnel
'cause this Graduate's spot is on the way.

09:26.880 --> 09:29.750
Right, you mentioned you couldn't keep them at home,

09:29.750 --> 09:33.540
since even sealed,
they could affect everyone on our block.

09:33.920 --> 09:39.040
Right. That's why I keep them in isolated areas
and go get them when I need them.

09:39.290 --> 09:42.250
With a few exceptions, like the High Priest.

09:42.540 --> 09:47.540
<b>WIDE VIEW</b>

09:42.540 --> 09:47.540
<b>DETAILS</b>

09:42.750 --> 09:44.250
So, where are we going?

09:44.670 --> 09:47.380
O City, the bank of the T River.

09:48.500 --> 09:50.380
Looks like the middle of nowhere.

09:50.580 --> 09:53.330
Looks can be deceiving.
It's an incredibly important location.

09:53.670 --> 09:54.880
How so?

09:56.290 --> 10:02.460
Spiritual energy flows down here.
Some call them, "dragon veins."

10:00.500 --> 10:02.830
<b>CITY</b>

10:00.500 --> 10:02.830
<b>CITY</b>

10:00.500 --> 10:02.830
<b>CITY</b>

10:00.500 --> 10:02.830
<b>CITY</b>

10:03.000 --> 10:05.750
Here, it overlaps with the Tachikawa Fault.

10:07.460 --> 10:12.000
Spirits will weaken and die if they don't eat other spirits,

10:12.790 --> 10:16.630
so by keeping it here, the spiritual energy flow
keeps it from weakening.

10:17.250 --> 10:21.210
I went there with Eiko once before to get it set up there.

10:21.500 --> 10:24.960
Come to think of it, we came out here a while back.

10:25.210 --> 10:30.790
Okay, so I understand all that,
but what kind of spirit is this Graduate?

10:31.250 --> 10:36.080
If it's as dangerous as the High Priest,
then we probably need to prep, right?

10:36.330 --> 10:36.960
Mhm.

10:38.000 --> 10:41.380
This Graduate isn't an evil spirit,

10:41.710 --> 10:44.920
but it's incredibly dangerous.

10:46.790 --> 10:50.830
It's the spirit of a man who fought
in the South Pacific during the war.

10:52.630 --> 10:56.750
While alive, he was said to be so resilient
as to be unkillable,

10:57.040 --> 10:59.500
and his spirit honors that trait even in death.

11:00.170 --> 11:03.380
But the real danger we need to watch out for...

11:03.920 --> 11:11.170
...are the souls of the hundreds of enemy soldiers
he killed that still cling to him, seeking their vengeance.

11:13.330 --> 11:17.500
These soldiers are constantly picking away at him,

11:18.040 --> 11:22.790
but his high resilience allows him
to quickly recover from any damage or curse upon him,

11:22.960 --> 11:28.670
so even if he runs out of energy,
he can't pass on; he's stuck in this world.

11:29.540 --> 11:36.080
I promised to help him pass on
if he agreed to lend me his strength now and then,

11:36.630 --> 11:39.080
so we're on friendly terms.

11:39.830 --> 11:47.290
But he can't control the other spirits
leaking out from around his seal.

11:48.790 --> 11:53.790
So we'll put an extra seal on him with black rope
made from the hair of that one spirit.

11:53.790 --> 11:56.750
That'll stop the soldiers from leaking out
so we can emancipate him.

11:57.000 --> 11:58.330
"Emancipate"...?

11:58.670 --> 12:00.040
Take him out with us.

12:00.170 --> 12:05.080
We're releasing him from the confines of a world
from where he cannot pass on.

12:05.330 --> 12:07.380
The word seemed fitting.

12:06.580 --> 12:09.500
<b>EMANCIPATE</b>

12:11.170 --> 12:13.960
Anyways, we need to stop to buy stuff.

12:15.880 --> 12:19.960
We'll be up against soldiers who died on the battlefield,
all desperate for water.

12:21.130 --> 12:25.170
If we have water on us,
they should leave us alone for the most part.

12:25.830 --> 12:30.250
Those spirits aren't evil, but they're still soldiers at heart.

12:30.420 --> 12:34.080
They won't hesitate to kill us,
if only because that's how they were taught to survive.

12:35.420 --> 12:38.920
They're much more driven to kill
than your most bloodthirsty murderer,

12:39.830 --> 12:41.790
so don't let your guard down around them.

12:54.130 --> 12:55.000
This way.

12:58.880 --> 13:00.920
Wait, do you hear that?

13:01.500 --> 13:03.580
It doesn't sound like bugs...

13:20.330 --> 13:22.750
What's going on with that mannequin?

13:24.000 --> 13:28.420
There are marks all over its torso.

13:32.250 --> 13:33.920
It's gone quiet.

13:34.380 --> 13:35.630
They're looking at us.

13:35.630 --> 13:36.130
Huh?

13:43.960 --> 13:45.290
The TV turned on.

13:45.880 --> 13:48.330
But how is it getting power...?

13:55.000 --> 13:59.670
I am the Breakwater... of the Pacific!

14:42.170 --> 14:46.000
The light from the TV shows us their shadows.

14:47.290 --> 14:50.210
That way, anyone can see the spirits.

14:51.170 --> 14:54.330
The Graduate is warning us.

15:04.330 --> 15:05.170
Kei-kun!

15:07.710 --> 15:10.040
Wh-what the...?

15:10.330 --> 15:13.000
It hurts. I'm hot.

15:13.170 --> 15:15.830
I'm so thirsty I could die.

15:16.080 --> 15:18.250
I need water...

15:46.670 --> 15:47.420
I...

15:47.880 --> 15:51.750
...am the Breakwater of the Pacific!

16:03.670 --> 16:05.540
It's so hot...

16:06.630 --> 16:10.790
Thirsty... So thirsty...

16:10.790 --> 16:12.790
Water!

16:23.580 --> 16:26.630
Everyone on both sides is starving and dying of thirst...

16:35.790 --> 16:39.040
When will this battle be over...?

16:51.210 --> 16:52.000
Keitaro.

16:53.250 --> 16:54.500
Stop, Keitaro!

16:57.040 --> 16:59.920
Huh? What? Why am I...?

17:00.880 --> 17:02.130
Did I drink it?!

17:03.210 --> 17:07.170
We'll be up against soldiers who died
on the battlefield, all desperate for water.

17:08.040 --> 17:11.920
If we have water on us,
they should leave us alone for the most part.

17:17.880 --> 17:18.540
Kei-kun!

17:18.540 --> 17:19.080
This isn't good.

17:23.210 --> 17:24.250
What's happening?

17:24.790 --> 17:26.790
It doesn't feel like hands...

17:27.210 --> 17:31.960
The doll's keeping it from hurting me, but what is it?
What's it doing to me?!

17:38.420 --> 17:41.460
Wait, are those...

17:42.210 --> 17:43.210
teeth marks?!

17:44.040 --> 17:46.750
It's trying to rip me open to... drink?

17:46.960 --> 17:49.250
To quench their thirst with my blood!

18:08.750 --> 18:11.920
They're all being drawn to Kei-kun!

18:15.790 --> 18:18.830
If we put the extra seal on the Graduate,
that should save him!

18:19.130 --> 18:21.790
Yayoi-chan, where's the Graduate's doll?!

18:22.170 --> 18:23.380
In the mannequin's head!

18:39.290 --> 18:43.500
The Graduate heals incredibly fast,

18:44.130 --> 18:48.960
but being constantly picked away
at would eventually destroy the doll sealing it.

18:49.960 --> 18:54.250
That's why I put it in the mannequin,
to keep it from taking too much damage.

18:55.380 --> 18:56.250
Yayoi-chan?

18:58.790 --> 19:00.580
Eiko, bring it here!

19:00.750 --> 19:01.460
Right!

19:18.790 --> 19:19.880
Yayoi-chan!

19:20.380 --> 19:21.210
Catch!

19:22.670 --> 19:23.420
Keitaro!

19:25.670 --> 19:26.460
A net?

19:26.790 --> 19:28.460
The black rope!

19:28.630 --> 19:29.790
It's all yours!

19:56.210 --> 19:57.580
Did we seal it?

19:58.170 --> 19:58.960
Yeah.

20:02.170 --> 20:03.880
We made it, somehow...

20:06.710 --> 20:11.710
We've successfully retrieved our Graduate.
Good work, you two.

20:12.580 --> 20:16.380
Thanks. Now, we can finally take a brea-

20:15.250 --> 20:16.380
Let's head to our true destination.

20:18.750 --> 20:22.630
Look, I'm already super exhausted...

20:32.920 --> 20:36.960
Hang in there. You should have
the most stamina out of all of us.

20:38.040 --> 20:39.920
I'm trying...

20:52.540 --> 20:53.960
Did I just imagine that?

20:55.330 --> 21:00.210
A supernatural phenomenon happened
so close to me, I could reach out and touch it!

21:00.630 --> 21:03.170
I was so terrified, but...

21:07.000 --> 21:09.170
...my heart's going to leap out of my chest!

21:09.630 --> 21:13.830
If I'd taken one step closer, I could've smelled it!

21:16.500 --> 21:20.130
How is it? All fixed up, Yayoi-chan?

21:20.130 --> 21:23.920
Yup. This'll keep us safe, no matter what might happen.

21:23.920 --> 21:27.920
I don't want anything to happen to us, though...

21:28.920 --> 21:32.380
Okay, next up: Old F Tunnel!

21:32.380 --> 21:33.790
Let's ghooo...

21:33.790 --> 21:34.790
...ooost!

23:22.630 --> 23:30.830
After arriving at the Old F Tunnel,
Yayoi and Keitaro get separated from Eiko.

23:31.500 --> 23:35.880
In their stead, appears a young woman.

23:36.580 --> 23:38.920
Is she a mere stranger, or...?
